<title>JAPAN: Japan average rates on time deposits.</title>
<headline>Japan average rates on time deposits.</headline>
<dateline>TOKYO 1997-06-18</dateline>
<text>
<p>Average rates on time deposits of more than 10 million yen in the week to June 11 as released by the Bank of Japan on Wednesday</p>
<p>    one mth	0.34 (0.34)	 one year     0.43 (0.41)</p>
<p>    three mths   0.34 (0.34)	 two years    0.65 (0.63)</p>
<p>    six mths     0.35 (0.35)	 three years  1.10 (1.09)</p>
<p>Average rates on time deposits of three to 10 million yen:</p>
<p>    one mth	0.30 (0.30)	 one year     0.38 (0.36)</p>
<p>    three mths   0.30 (0.30)	 two years    0.60 (0.58)</p>
<p>    six mths     0.30 (0.30)	 three years  1.05 (1.03)</p>
<p>Average rates on time deposits of less than three million</p>
<p>yen:</p>
<p>    one mth	0.25 (0.25)	 one year     0.33 (0.32)</p>
<p>    three mths   0.25 (0.25)	 two years    0.55 (0.53)</p>
<p>    six mths     0.25 (0.25)	 three years  1.00 (0.98)</p>
<p>Average rates on certificates of deposit, Jun 09 - Jun 13:</p>
<p>    less than 30 days  0.56 (0.56)   120-150 days  0.60 (0.57)</p>
<p>    30-60 days	   0.58 (0.58)   150-180 days  0.67 (0.63)</p>
<p>    60-90 days	   0.59 (0.59)   180-360 days  0.73 (0.64)</p>
<p>    90-120 days	  0.60 (0.60)   over 360 days 0.80 (0.80)</p>
